Fix GDMS double-counting a redespatched device (v0.123)

Dan tested the per-order manual GDMS assign again today and got
"2 device(s) assigned" for an order with only one device on it (an
HT801 V2). GdmsEndOfDayService#runForMovements() built its batch by
iterating every matching DESPATCH StockMovement and adding that
movement's StockItem to the list, with no deduplication - but a
single StockItem can genuinely have more than one DESPATCH movement
against it: despatch, OrderReversalService#reverseToDespatch() (which
deliberately never touches gdmsSyncedAt - see that class's own
comments), despatch again. Both DESPATCH movements point at the same
StockItem, so its one real MAC address went into the /assign batch
twice, and both our own devicesAssigned count and GDMS's own success
count reflected that duplicate.

Fixed by deduplicating on StockItem id (a HashSet of seen ids) before
a StockItem is ever added to a company's batch, regardless of how
many DESPATCH movements reference it.

Also confirmed, while looking at this, that untracked items (e.g. the
RJ11 BT adaptor that ships alongside an HT801 V2) are already handled
correctly and needed no change: DespatchService still creates a
StockMovement/StockItem for a NONE-tracking product (PickingService's
quantity-pick path), but it has no macAddress, and
runForMovements() already skips any item with a blank/null MAC before
it's ever added to a batch - so an untracked item is silently excluded
and never blocks or fails the assign for the tracked items in the same
order.

gdms-api-findings.md (project doc) updated with both confirmations.

